    {
      "post_id": "91619",
      "author_handle": "CoffeeAddict",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 years 1 month ago",
      "body": "Hi everyone,\nI'm Kellie I'm 26 and I have an 8 year old son, for ages I thought I was done with having kids, I had a terrible pregnancy and delivery with my son. It was a horrible relationship and I ended up being a single parent for many years. When I met my now husband he also didn't want kids so we happily settled as a family of 3. Now the last few months we have been getting niggling feelings of wanting to have a baby. If i was to be lucky and get pregnant quickly we would be looking at there being at least 9 years between the kids. Am I crazy for wanting to do baby stuff all over again? Does anyone else have kids with big ages gaps that can offer tips or advice.\nThanks.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10887/#91619",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/db35ebf3d708572bc8ff.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10887/",
